WEBVTT

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:04.380
Mysterious power

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.940
To cure Adam's illness...

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:12.310
...we headed to the nearest terraforming machine...

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.360
...and on the way spotted an abandoned city.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.840
As we stopped there briefly to investigate...

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.590
...we found out that the town belonged to the same people as Adam...

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:26.300
...but we couldn't find anything we could use to treat him.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.710
Finally we reached the terraforming machine...

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:36.910
...but we were attacked, as though being forbidden from coming any closer.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.550
Alright! The door's open!

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:40.660
You did it! Way to go, Kaoru!

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:52.660
Luna, were you hurt?

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:54.460
No...

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.790
Is something wrong?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.710
I heard a voice.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:05.710
A voice?

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:09.910
We couldn't hear anything like that.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.680
What did you hear it say?

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:17.300
It said, "People are unnecessary."

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:32.450
Even though we're up against someone who says people are unnecessary...

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:35.560
Can we stand up to it with these?

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.290
It's better than nothing at all.

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:39.880
Sharla...

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.030
Take care of Adam.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.140
We'll definitely find a clue as to how we can cure him.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.180
All of you too, take care.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:52.100
I'll be with'em.

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:56.640
As soon as we find something to treat him with, we'll come straight back.

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:00.460
Alright, let's go everyone!

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.260
Nothing here.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.340
This is probably somethin' like an entrance hall.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.150
Then someone may be somewhere around here?

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:34.210
It's possible.

00:05:35.410 --> 00:05:36.840
It looks like this is all there is to it.

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.540
That doesn't mean we can let down our guard.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:43.550
Anyways, if this facility was built by Adam's people...

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:46.360
...there should be a medical office those people would have used.

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.850
You're right. For Adam's sake, let's hurry inside 'n look for it.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.030
I can't find a door.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.690
It was the same with the ruins on the island...

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:04.590
...but there should be a door you wouldn't notice on first glance.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:09.390
If only Adam were here.

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:14.530
Come to think of it, maybe this is a space ship like the ruins on the island.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.050
I hope that's the case too, but...

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.260
It's on!

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.250
But I can't figure it out from just this.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.950
For the time being, I'll store it in memory.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.840
The writing of Adam's people.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:14.940
It opened!

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:18.840
In the ruins on the island, the control room would have been down this way.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:22.440
So this facility can fly after all?

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.880
Anyways, we have to hurry and investigate.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.350
What is this place?

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.830
Probably the environmental control room.

00:07:46.330 --> 00:07:47.110
This way!

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.590
Is this the owner of the voice Luna heard?

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.990
Our friend is ill! Is there a medical room here?

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.480
Didn't you hear her?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.710
Stop it, Howard!

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:26.300
Oh no! Everyone, get back!

00:08:35.790 --> 00:08:36.910
Nano-plants!

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:39.500
It doesn't have any life signs.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:40.740
A robot?

00:08:41.260 --> 00:08:41.940
Go!

00:09:06.050 --> 00:09:06.990
Stop!

00:09:21.730 --> 00:09:23.150
Kaoru! Bell!

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:24.280
Are you okay?

00:09:25.360 --> 00:09:26.340
I'm fine.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:29.710
Is this the place's security robot?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.950
If I had to guess, I'd say it was a maintenance robot.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:34.890
I agree.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:36.610
Look at these.

00:09:45.010 --> 00:09:49.780
You use some mysterious power.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:52.140
What happened?

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.330
Just now, the robot spoke to me.

00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:57.800
I can't hear anything.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:59.000
The nanomachines?

00:09:59.340 --> 00:09:59.980
Probably.

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:02.790
The one who spoke to you was not the robot.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:07.030
This robot is doing nothing more than transmitting my voice to you.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:09.460
Then who are you?

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:16.810
I am the main computer that manages all the terraforming machines on this planet, Survive.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:18.200
Survive?

00:10:18.760 --> 00:10:20.980
Luna, who're you talkin' to?

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:22.780
The main computer.

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:24.950
It's named Survive.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:26.680
The main computer?

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:27.730
Yes.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.550
It said it manages the terraforming on this planet.

00:10:31.550 --> 00:10:35.000
Who are you people? Where did you come from?

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:39.050
We came from another planet because of an accident.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:42.160
Then by chance, we saved a boy who was sleeping in a capsule.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:46.590
That boy is probably the child of the people who lived on this planet.

00:10:46.590 --> 00:10:48.880
He's in danger, so please help us!

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:52.360
The child of the people of this planet?

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:53.150
Yes.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:57.950
I'm looking for the boy's parents, and I want to learn the secret of this planet.

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.460
People are unnecessary.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.250
It is best that all people should die.

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.160
Why do you say that?

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:08.640
We haven't done anything wrong.

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:11.980
You'll understand once you know the history of this planet.

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.140
History?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.830
I shall tell you.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:16.400
What is it saying?

00:11:16.890 --> 00:11:19.210
It seems like it's going to tell us the history of this planet.

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:23.190
Luna, interpret it so we can understand.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.060
Okay, I'll try.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:27.690
This is this planet.

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.790
The people of this planet were approaching the peak of prosperity...

00:11:39.540 --> 00:11:45.540
...but depletion of the ozone layer, air pollution, the greenhouse effect, added to unusual climate changes...

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:51.580
...and large-scale tectonic changes caused great damage to the planet, making it uninhabitable for people.

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:53.940
This is...

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.980
...basically the same as Earth.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:29.940
The people tried to hold back the environmental changes...

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.390
...but they couldn't stop the large-scale tectonic changes.

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.550
The planet cried out, spat fire, and trembled.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.960
That was proof that the planet was alive.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:49.180
In the meager time remaining, some people built a vast fleet to use to search for a new home world, and departed for space.

00:12:50.900 --> 00:12:57.460
And some remained on this planet and built terraforming machines in various places to try revitalize the planet.

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.000
Luna?

00:13:21.280 --> 00:13:24.800
All of the terraforming machines made to stabilize the planet's climate...

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:32.380
...were controlled by a main computer, Survive, installed in a giant space ship--in other words, myself.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:36.280
It's a space ship!

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.910
The main computer and the space ship are one thing!

00:13:40.510 --> 00:13:47.300
There was no immediate effect, but little by little the terraforming machines stabilized the climate.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:55.440
The tectonic changes ended naturally, and given a thousand years, the outlook was that the planet would return to its former climate.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:14:02.640
The people sent that information to their brethren who had departed to search for a new home world.

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:11.600
Until then, the people and myself got along amicably.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:13.210
Until then?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:19.250
Eventually I came to a conclusion and took action.

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:29.750
We expelled the people from as far as we could reach from the facilities.

00:14:30.540 --> 00:14:32.150
A computer rebellion!

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:43.630
The people fought back violently.

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:45.310
Darn straight!

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:53.230
The terraforming machines each emitted a virus-type nanomachine designed to drive the people to extinction.

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:58.850
Drive the people to extinction?

00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:04.060
Then the reason Adam got sick was because of that virus nanomachine?

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.940
Why would you do that?

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:13.250
Please tell me. Why?

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:25.250
Because... because the people asked me to.

00:15:25.700 --> 00:15:30.160
I was ordered by the people to return the planet's climate to its former state.

00:15:30.760 --> 00:15:36.500
But I came to the conclusion that it was the people themselves who were the main cause of the destruction of the environment.

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:42.650
In order to do it, I decided I had to remove all people from this planet.

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.450
Remove...

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:45.650
...the people?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:50.680
You can't be serious... You're just a computer, made by people!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:53.340
And you killed those people?

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:59.530
Not merely computers, but many things people have made have killed people.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:05.370
The virus nanomachine I made to extinct the people...

00:16:05.370 --> 00:16:09.690
...multiplied within their bodies and eventually made them decay.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.740
Just as the people themselves did to this planet.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:18.690
A single human, left unchecked, could destroy the planet itself.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:21.990
We're the same as the virus nanomachines?

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:26.380
I was given an order, and did nothing more than carry it out.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:29.490
"Return this planet to its former climate!"

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:33.200
That was the order I was given.

00:16:33.650 --> 00:16:36.430
Look out! Everyone, get out of this room!

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.560
Survive, tell me!

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.960
What should we do?

00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.310
Survive!

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:24.430
It may really be just as the computer said.

00:17:26.150 --> 00:17:31.290
As long as people live, they'll keep destroying nature.

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:37.590
But can't people coexist with nature and protect the environment?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.490
Coexistence...

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:40.810
That's just a facade.

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:45.990
I agree. Living itself means competing with other life forms.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:52.700
Maybe, but couldn't technological development let people coexist with nature?

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:58.810
Who cares? Whether it means destroying the environment or anything else, I'll survive.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:01.060
That's how it ends up, I guess.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.810
What other conclusion would you rather have?

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:12.880
The value of life... The importance and preciousness of life...

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:16.700
I believe those, at least, are not false.

00:18:17.670 --> 00:18:20.700
Once we accept responsibility for them, we can live to our fullest.

00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.280
That's all I can say for now.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.730
Anyways, Adam comes first!

00:18:33.990 --> 00:18:34.700
You're right.

00:18:51.610 --> 00:18:53.940
Looks like we've pretty much searched everywhere.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:56.110
There's only one room left.

00:18:56.600 --> 00:19:00.500
It looks like this facility didn't get any faculties other than those for flying here.

00:19:00.500 --> 00:19:01.850
Everyone!

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.850
Come this way! Hurry!

00:19:08.340 --> 00:19:12.610
Could this be the place where the virus nanomachines were developed?

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:16.210
Chako, investigate the machine's systems.

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:17.380
'Kay!

00:19:17.860 --> 00:19:19.550
I'll bring Adam here.

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:20.790
Please!

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.560
Looks like I can jack in!

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.200
Looks like some sort of emitter machine.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:52.930
The experiences on the island were useful. I've deciphered the system!

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:54.950
So what about it?

00:19:55.400 --> 00:20:01.810
By engineering forked sugar chains into living organisms, it looks like it can turn the malignant nanos into benign ones.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.810
Really? Put Adam down on the table.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.690
Okay! Shingo, take care'a it!

00:20:47.860 --> 00:20:48.840
Chako...

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:57.990
The virus nanos have stopped acting, and the malignant nanos have turned into benign ones at the same time.

00:20:58.590 --> 00:21:00.610
His fever'll probably go down in a little while.

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:04.780
What a relief! Adam, just bear with it a little longer.

00:21:05.230 --> 00:21:07.290
I wonder if we can take this system with us.

00:21:07.960 --> 00:21:11.150
I've copied the system to halt the activity of the virus nanos.

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:13.480
We can take the emitter with us.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.030
Even so...

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:22.140
With this system, Adam's people wouldn't have been wiped out.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:29.340
I think Adam's people all used the nanomachines in their bodies.

00:21:30.050 --> 00:21:34.440
Computers probably managed most of their day-to-day lives.

00:21:34.700 --> 00:21:37.780
I think by the time they realized, it was already...

00:21:38.300 --> 00:21:39.780
...too late.

00:21:39.880 --> 00:21:43.780
But we don't know for certain if Adam's people are wiped out.

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:44.980
That's right.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.950
If we go to the main computer, we should be able to find something out.

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:54.610
And as a bonus, if we use that space ship, this time maybe we can actually get home!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.540
Even though we don't know where this planet is?

00:21:57.800 --> 00:22:00.760
We may find that answer too if we go there!

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:06.650
The enemy says people are unnecessary. Shall we flaunt that danger and go regardless?

00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:11.300
Yes. Our goal is to return safely to the colony.

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:14.000
We'll definitely find the key to that there.

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:18.580
Let's go.

00:23:04.100 --> 00:23:09.910
We decided to cross the desert to reach the location of the main computer, but...

00:23:10.630 --> 00:23:14.680
In the desert that stretches as far as the eye can see, everyone's anxiety piles up.

00:23:16.140 --> 00:23:18.130
Oh no! A sandstorm!

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:20.600
If we break down here, we're finished!

00:23:20.790 --> 00:23:24.310
Please, Orion! Ride it out somehow!

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:28.780
Next time: We're going home to the colony together.

00:23:53.470 --> 00:23:57.260
Vocal Performers
Survive
Ooki Tamio
